-- title:
--   Integrality over A[j₀] for the Γ₀(N)×Γ₁(ℓ) moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $\ell$ a prime with $5\le\ell$, and $N$ a nonzero natural number, with the images of $\ell$ and $N$ units in $A$. Three compatibility hypotheses are assumed, each for all $A$-algebras $T$, Weierstrass curves $W$ over $T$ and variable changes $C$: (i) if a quadruple $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ over $T$ satisfies the affine equation of $W$ at $(x_P,y_P)$, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_P)=0$, $x_Q=x_P$ and $y_Q=y_P$, then its transform `D.variableChange C` satisfies the same conditions for $C\bullet W$; (ii) for all $p,k$ and $h\in T[X]$, the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (for $p^k=2$: $\deg h\le1$, $h$ has coefficient $1$ in degree $1$ and $h\mid W.\Psi_2^{\,2}$; otherwise: $\deg h\le\varphi(p^k)/2$, the coefficient of $h$ in degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$ is $1$, $h\cdot W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}\mid W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and $h\mid W.\mathrm{smulNumerator}\,a\,(\varphi(p^k)/2)\,h$ for all $a$ with $2\le a\le (p^k-1)/2$ and $p\nmid a$) is preserved by $h\mapsto$ `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; (iii) for all $d,n$, $h\in T[X]$ and $x\in T$, if $h$ divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x` $=\prod_{a=1}^{(\ell-1)/2}\bigl(\Phi_n\cdot(\Psi_a^2)(x)-(\Phi_a)(x)\cdot\Psi_n^2\bigr)$, then `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` divides `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓ n (u^{-2}(x-r))`. Let $P_0$ be an abstract fine moduli package for the moduli datum of the rigid problem built from the product of the $\Gamma_0$-component at level $N$ (tuples of polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $N$, each satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` at the corresponding exact power), the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point component, and the trivial component (a one-point set with vacuous level condition), cut out by the link condition that whenever $\ell\mid N$ the $\ell$-th polynomial divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓ (ℓ^(N.factorization ℓ - 1)) x_P`; thus $P_0$ consists of a commutative $A$-algebra $B_0=P_0.B_0$, a universal point `univ` over $B_0$ (a curve with unit discriminant together with such level data, modulo variable change), and the property that every point of the problem over any $A$-algebra $T$ is induced by a unique $A$-algebra map $B_0\to T$. Assuming $B_0$ is of finite type over $A$, the conclusion is that $B_0$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra of $B_0$ generated by $P_0.j_0$, the $j$-invariant of the universal point.
--
--   This is the finiteness step in the construction of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(\ell)$ in the Weierstrass-equation presentation: the universal ring of the level problem is integral over $A[j]$, so that the curve is finite over the $j$-line. It is used in the proof of the existence of such a moduli package, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_levelModuliPackageAbs_trivial_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_levelModuliPackageAbs_trivial_rigidDataH1Pow), and rests on a valuation-theoretic criterion for integrality together with the descent of a Weierstrass model with its level data to a discrete valuation ring when the $j$-invariant is integral there.
